    <DataNode elementId="AT1G31070-MONOMER" textLabel="UDP-N-acetylglucosamine diphosphorylase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q940S3" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="395" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">UDP-N-acetylglucosamine (UDP-GlcNAc) is an essential precursor for glycoprotein and glycolipid biosynthesis in plants and it can also serve as a regulatory modification on signaling protein. This enzyme, GlcNAc1pUT1, is capable of synthesizing |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE| (UDP-GlcNAc) from |FRAME: UTP| and |FRAME: N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE-1-P| &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [20557289]|. It can also catalyze the reverse reaction using |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE UDP-GlcNAc| and the less common 4-epimer, |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-GALACTOSAMINE| (UDP-GalNAc) |CITS: [20557289]|. The enzyme requires divalent cations, such as |FRAME: MG+2| or |FRAME: MN+2| to be active, but cannot utilize |FRAME: CA+2|. The enzyme maintains GlcNAc1pUT activity across a wide range of pH values and temperatures, but, shows optimum activity at a pH 7.6-8.0 and a temperature of 30-37 &amp;deg;C |CITS: [20557289]|. The enzyme appeared to be quite specific and did not show activity &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; with several other nucleotide triphosphates or other sugar-1-phosphates |CITS: [20557289]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G31070-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G31070.2" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q940S3" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="N-acetylglucosamine-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase 1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="UDP-N-acetylgalactosamine diphosphorylase 1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-T9-1226, RXN-12844" />
