    <DataNode elementId="AT3G24090-MONOMER" textLabel="AT3G24090-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G24090-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="395" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="AUQT-1">GFAT is a L-glutamine D-fructose- 6-phosphate amidotransferase that likely plays a role in |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE UDP-&amp;alpha;-&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetyl-D-glucosamine| biosynthesis based on an &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; assay |CITS:SHIBATANI09|. Interestingly, in contrast to a GFAT from chlorella virus PCBV-1, overexpression of the Arabidopsis enzyme in tobacco cell cultures did not lead to an increased accumulation of hexosamines. However, other euakaryotic GFATs with similar sequences are subject to |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE UDP-&amp;alpha;-&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetyl-D-glucosamine|-mediated negative feedback |CITS: [16408321]|. If the Arabidopsis enzyme is subject to the same inihibition, it could explain the apparently contradictory &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; behavior of this enzyme |CITS: [SHIBATANI09]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G24090-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-9492" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G24090.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G24090" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12000639" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16408321" />
    </DataNode>
